name: "Sora 2 API Fixes: 20-second limit, HD format, multi-segment generation"
description: |
  Three interconnected fixes for the Sora 2 video generation app:
  1. Enable 16s and 20s video generation (API now supports it)
  2. Fix HD format (1920x1080/1080x1920) — requires sora-2-pro model + validation
  3. Fix multi-segment generation stopping — timeout + retry + polling rate fix

---

## Goal

**Feature Goal**: Fix three production bugs in the Sora 2 video generation app so users can generate longer videos (up to 20s), HD 1080p videos (with sora-2-pro), and multi-segment videos that complete reliably without hanging.

**Deliverable**:
1. Updated validation in `proxy-create-video.ts` to accept `['4', '8', '12', '16', '20']` seconds
2. Updated UI dropdowns in `PromptForm.tsx` and `PromptEditor.tsx` to offer 16s and 20s options
3. Fixed HD format: auto-select `sora-2-pro` model when HD size is chosen; add server-side size+model validation
4. Fixed polling in `openaiService.ts`: slower interval, 20-minute timeout, retry-safe error handling
5. Fixed multi-segment loop in `App.tsx`: don't abort all segments on one failure; add per-segment timeout; informative logs
6. Added comprehensive logging throughout for debugging

**Success Definition**:
- User can select 16s or 20s video duration and generate successfully
- User can select 1920x1080 or 1080x1920 and app automatically uses `sora-2-pro`
- Multi-segment generation completes even if one segment takes longer than usual
- Stuck jobs (> 20 min) time out gracefully with user-visible error instead of hanging forever
- Console logs clearly show what's happening at each step for debugging

## User Persona

**Target User**: Developer/creator using the Sora 2 app to generate AI videos

**Use Case**:
- Generating 20-second cinematic scenes for content creation
- Creating HD 1080p videos for professional use
- Generating multi-segment videos (2-5 clips) for extended narratives

**Pain Points Addressed**:
- Videos silently fail when HD size is selected (wrong model auto-selected)
- Multi-segment generation freezes indefinitely with no error
- Max video length is limited to 12s despite OpenAI now supporting 20s

## Why

- OpenAI announced 20-second clip support in March 2026 (new capability)
- HD format is completely broken (API rejects `sora-2` model with `1920x1080` size)
- Multi-segment generation hangs due to: (a) 2-second polling is too aggressive, (b) no timeout for stuck jobs, (c) first segment failure aborts everything
- Users have no visibility into what's going wrong (poor logging)

## What

### User-Visible Behaviors

1. **Duration dropdown**: Shows 4s, 8s, 12s, 16s, 20s options (was: only 4s, 8s, 12s)
2. **HD sizes**: Selecting 1920x1080 or 1080x1920 works reliably (was: silently fails)
3. **Model auto-selection**: App automatically uses `sora-2-pro` when HD size selected (transparent to user)
4. **Multi-segment**: All segments complete or fail individually with retry; doesn't freeze
5. **Timeout feedback**: "Video generation timed out after 20 minutes. Please try again." when stuck
6. **Console logs**: Rich debug logs at every step for development troubleshooting

### Success Criteria

- [ ] Selecting `20` seconds and submitting generates a valid 20-second video
- [ ] Selecting `1920x1080` size correctly uses `sora-2-pro` model in API call
- [ ] Selecting `1920x1080` with size `sora-2` is blocked at proxy level with clear error
- [ ] Multi-segment generation (3+ segments) completes without freezing
- [ ] A simulated stuck job (mock) times out at 20 minutes with error message
- [ ] All generation steps log to console with `[OpenAI]`, `[Segment]`, `[Poll]` prefixes
- [ ] TypeScript compiles without errors: `npm run build`
- [ ] ESLint passes: `npm run lint`

