### Desired Codebase Changes (files modified, none created)

All fixes are in existing files — no new files needed.

### Known Gotchas of This Codebase

```typescript
// CRITICAL: proxy-create-video.ts is a Vercel Edge Function
// - Only Web APIs available (no Node.js fs, path, etc.)
// - Edge functions have strict execution limits
// - FormData handling is native (no multer)

// CRITICAL: Model auto-selection for Pro/HD sizes
// The code in sceneBuilderStore.ts hardcodes model: 'sora-2'
// The code in App.tsx hardcodes model: 'sora-2'
// Both MUST use 'sora-2-pro' when any of these Pro sizes are chosen:
//   '1792x1024', '1024x1792', '1920x1080', '1080x1920'
// Implement a helper: getModelForSize(size: string): string

// IMPORTANT: ALL size values in PromptForm.tsx ARE VALID OpenAI API values:
// - '1280x720' — valid, sora-2 compatible
// - '1792x1024' — valid, sora-2-pro ONLY (labeled "1024p Pro")
// - '720x1280'  — valid, sora-2 compatible
// - '1024x1792' — valid, sora-2-pro ONLY (labeled "Portrait Pro")
// The PromptForm.tsx size values are CORRECT, they just need auto model selection.
// PromptEditor.tsx has different Pro sizes: '1920x1080' and '1080x1920' — also valid sora-2-pro.

// FULL list of confirmed valid size values (OpenAI API):
// sora-2:     '480x480', '480x854', '854x480', '720x720', '720x1280', '1280x720', '1080x1080'
// sora-2-pro: '720x1280', '1280x720', '1792x1024', '1024x1792', '1920x1080', '1080x1920'

// CRITICAL: inputReference (frame continuity) image size
// When using inputReference for frame continuity between segments,
// the JPEG blob extracted by videoFrameExtractor must match the video's size exactly.
// Currently extractLastFrame() uses canvas at video dimensions — this is correct
// as long as the video itself is the correct size. Being off by 1 pixel causes error.

// CRITICAL: pollUntilComplete is used in:
// - App.tsx (home page, multi-segment)
// - sceneBuilderStore.ts (createNewScene, extendScene)
// - remixService.ts (autoRemix)
// A timeout in pollUntilComplete will propagate correctly to all callers.

// CRITICAL: downloadVideo in openaiService.ts downloads from OpenAI CDN directly
// This bypasses the Vercel proxy — requires CORS support from OpenAI CDN.
// Currently works because OpenAI CDN allows direct browser access.

// CRITICAL: The seconds param in API is always a STRING not a number
// - formData.seconds is number (UI)
// - CreateVideoRequest.seconds is string (API)
// - Conversion: String(formData.seconds)

// NOTE: planningService.ts also has a comment referencing only 4/8/12 seconds
// Update the comment there too when adding 16/20 second support.
```

