## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- ❌ Don't change poll interval to something faster than 10 seconds (API rate limits)
- ❌ Don't set timeout shorter than 5 minutes (real generations can take 2-3 minutes)
- ❌ Don't log API keys or full prompts in console
- ❌ Don't create new files when existing files can be modified
- ❌ Don't change the HD size values to anything other than '1920x1080' / '1080x1920' for the direct OpenAI API
- ❌ Don't use async/await in Edge Functions without proper error wrapping
- ❌ Don't forget to update BOTH PromptForm.tsx (home) AND PromptEditor.tsx (scene builder)
- ❌ Don't hardcode model: 'sora-2' anywhere — always use getModelForSize(size)

## Root Cause Summary

### Why 20-second limit wasn't working
`proxy-create-video.ts:56` has `if (!['4', '8', '12'].includes(secondsStr))` — only 3 values. OpenAI added 16s and 20s in March 2026. Both the proxy validation AND the UI dropdowns need updating.

### Why HD format (1920x1080) fails
The PromptEditor.tsx creates scenes with `model: 'sora-2'` hardcoded (line 68), but OpenAI requires `sora-2-pro` for any Pro-sized resolution (`1792x1024`, `1024x1792`, `1920x1080`, `1080x1920`). The API returns a model compatibility error.
The PromptForm.tsx also hardcodes `model: 'sora-2'` in App.tsx (line 275), meaning even when a user picks "1024p Pro (1792x1024)" the request goes out with `sora-2` and fails.
NOTE: `1792x1024` and `1024x1792` ARE valid direct OpenAI API size values — the size labels in PromptForm are correct, only the model selection is broken.

### Why multi-segment generation stops
Three compounding issues:
1. **Polling too aggressive**: 2-second interval violates API guidance (10-20s recommended), may cause rate limiting
2. **No timeout**: `pollUntilComplete` loops forever — a job stuck in `in_progress` (known 5-7% failure rate) will freeze the entire UI forever
3. **Error propagation**: The `catch (segmentError)` block re-throws, aborting all remaining segments even if they could have succeeded
